      "message": "fix(motion): re-centre a pole axis only on an isotropic part, by area\n\nReview of PR #204: a 100 x 100 x 10 plate with a turned r5 boss at\n(20, 20) read as a trusted (0.667, 0.667, 0.333) axis. The trimmed half\nwas taken by facet count (the boss is 792 of 804 facets, 1.3 % of the\narea), and the plate's two-triangle faces put every normal line through\nits centre, which any line through it meets.\n\nThe least-trimmed-squares re-centring now takes the AREA-weighted\nmedian, requires the kept half to carry MIN_KEPT_SHARE of the answering\narea on MIN_KEPT facets (as axis_robust::reweigh does), and runs only\nwhen the normal moment is isotropic. Elsewhere the plain line's drag\nstays the evidence, as it was on main.\n\nPinned by a_plate_with_an_off_centre_boss_is_refused_by_name.\n\nRefs #152\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
